NULL CITY — license scope
Copyright (c) 2026 GOROman

This repository uses different licenses for different components:

1. MIT: Python scripts and other software outside fonts/null-font/.
   See LICENSES/MIT.txt.
2. CC BY 4.0: original hardware/manufacturing data (STL, 3MF, Blender),
   artwork and decals, design/configuration JSON, original renders, and
   project documentation, except the font package and third-party material.
   See LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt.
3. SIL OFL 1.1: the entire fonts/null-font/ package, including font binaries,
   glyph sources, font build/validation scripts, specimens and documentation.
   See fonts/null-font/OFL.txt. No Reserved Font Names are declared.
4. CC BY-SA 4.0: KiCad PCB/schematic data and derived design exports in
   hardware/nc03-controller/, which embed the Seeed XIAO land pattern.
   See hardware/nc03-controller/vendor/README.md and its retained license.
   Scripts and firmware remain MIT. Original enclosure/artwork stay CC BY 4.0.

The font package is the explicit exception to the MIT script license.
Fonts embedded in Blender/3MF or other documents retain their OFL license;
using the font does not change the license of the resulting document/artwork.
Copies of these license texts retain their original notices.

Third-party materials, including manufacturer PDFs in docs/references/,
manufacturer printer/filament profiles and bundled slicer metadata, retain
their original licenses and copyrights. The licenses above grant no new
rights to third-party material. See the reference manifest and source links.

Attribution example for original CC BY 4.0 assets:
"NULL CITY NC-03 by GOROman — https://github.com/GOROman/null-city —
CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)."
When sharing modifications, also describe what you changed.
